# Fine-grained commits

When the user asks to commit (or commit & push):

- Prefer **many small commits** over one large commit. The user reviews each commit separately.
- Split by independent concern (keybind vs script vs skill vs unrelated config). One logical change per commit.
- Do not bundle unrelated files just because they changed in the same session.
- If the split is ambiguous, propose a short commit list once, then proceed that way.
- Still only commit when explicitly asked. Never push unless asked.
- Keep each message scoped to that slice’s why (1–2 sentences).
